From 7af1ef86de0d927f027cb537060b828b1b1a7591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: makrohard
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:10:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(flash): save settings where they change

Some settings were changed in RAM without saving them. They only reached
flash because every transmission rewrote all settings afterwards, so a
change was lost if the node was switched off before its next HEY or
message:

- --aprsmc now saves like every other setting command.
- T-Deck: the standby and keyboard-backlight buttons in the header and
  SYM+L / SYM+K save the lock state (it is restored from flash at boot).
- T-Deck Pro: ALT+L, ALT+K, ALT+O, ALT+I and ALT+M save the changed
  backlight lock, keyboard lock, map and mute.
- A UTC offset received via the soft-serial XML is saved when it changes.
- ESP32: a new GPS fix is saved (save_position(), at most every 15 min).
  Without a fix the node sends the stored position, so the last fix has
  to survive a reboot.

Phone settings keep their protocol: values are committed by 0xF0 "Save
Settings" or by the 0x0A save flag; periodic phone positions are not
saved (phone_commands.cpp). T-Deck setup page values are committed by
its Save button.
